-- Milestone 1 — authentication and audit foundation.
--
-- The section above the "HAND-WRITTEN" banner is generated by Prisma. Everything
-- below it is hand-written, because Prisma cannot express CHECK constraints,
-- partial indexes, functions or triggers. Each hand-written object is named, and
-- an integration test asserts every name exists in the PostgreSQL catalogue, so
-- a future edit cannot quietly drop one.
--
-- On timestamps: Prisma emits `CURRENT_TIMESTAMP`, which in PostgreSQL is an
-- exact synonym for `transaction_timestamp()` — the transaction start time, not
-- the wall clock at statement execution. That is the intended semantic: every
-- row written in one transaction shares a timestamp, so a state change and its
-- audit row are provably simultaneous. The spelling is left as Prisma generates
-- it so schema-drift detection cannot produce a false positive on a synonym.
-- Session liveness comparisons deliberately use `clock_timestamp()` instead, but
-- those live in application SQL, not here.

